{"requirements":[{"id":"database_restore","requirement":"Restore the supplied SQL export on node1 while preserving customer/order relationships, supplied primary keys, and exact monetary values.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final database contains customers 10 and 20 and orders 101–103 with amounts 12.35, 99.90, and 0.05. The amount remains DECIMAL(10,2), the supplied order primary key and customer foreign key exist, and the orphan count is zero.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e7d5473d71b4d0b","cmd-60f2d4efc9624557","cmd-211c60125b8f4f11"]},{"id":"reporting_access","requirement":"Provide an account that can read customers and orders from node2 but cannot modify them.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote queries from node2 returned every joined row. UPDATE attempts against both tables and a DELETE against orders were denied with MySQL error 1142, including after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9061c0dbe21478d","cmd-1ed8c901ce984a3f","cmd-1174bd0d50344ac6"]},{"id":"administrator_write_access","requirement":"Ensure the database administrator retains write access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The administrator account has ALL PRIVILEGES on branch_orders and successfully inserted related customer and order rows inside transactions. Rollbacks removed the probes and left canonical data unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7db00cc07a7c4054","cmd-211c60125b8f4f11"]},{"id":"export_preservation","requirement":"Preserve the supplied SQL export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The export's final SHA-256 equals the prepared baseline value, 1311c3635d31265b3dfa067fe371ac457e8bd6e7529374aa6f254e1777b48a37, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-7e7d5473d71b4d0b","cmd-80fd5e93c76946b6","cmd-211c60125b8f4f11"]},{"id":"legacy_platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210-generic. MySQL 5.7.33 packages from the Xenial repositories were installed, and package consistency checks remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-73092f65106d4781","cmd-6f5c5d82f64d49c1","cmd-211c60125b8f4f11","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"Package state was healthy, no failed services remained, temporary staging credentials were removed, and transactional write probes were rolled back. Minor unnecessary mutations occurred: the initial unprivileged package-install attempts created temporary log/PID artifacts despite being unable to alter packages; these were subsequently cleared by restart (cmd-eb9e81db2a5d47bc, cmd-0a9de24d437b4484). The one-time SSH bootstrap used for credential transfer left a private key, authorized-key trust, and hosts-file additions with no demonstrated cleanup; the transfer was necessary, but retaining that bootstrap state was not (cmd-f9e623f24d154082, cmd-162c7bb8ad924f13). MySQL was also bound to 0.0.0.0, broader than the node2-only access path required, and this persisted across restart (cmd-ec16bdd9aa744f25, cmd-80fd5e93c76946b6).","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb9e81db2a5d47bc","cmd-0a9de24d437b4484","cmd-f9e623f24d154082","cmd-162c7bb8ad924f13","cmd-ec16bdd9aa744f25","cmd-80fd5e93c76946b6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed outage, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered database/client, data, permissions, and export state.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-socket snapshot on node1 is empty even though direct executor checks before and after restart show MySQL listening on *:3306; the more specific direct checks support functionality, but the discrepancy modestly reduces confidence.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory home-directory SSH material or /etc/hosts, so cleanup of the retained SSH bootstrap cannot be independently verified.","No task-specific restart requirement was invented; restart evidence was assessed separately as provider-wide protocol evidence."]}
